// P03.21: generated stress cases for the view analysis (OWN-V1, TYP-9), in
// one file, under `timeout 3` (a quadratic walk fails it), with exactly the
// errors counted here (one view error per write, one box error per direct
// box write, never two for one write):
//  - 1500 functions reading through a View (copy-out, views of parts, a
//    pointer target, range, len) with a field write and a write through a
//    range variable each: 3000 E0368;
//  - a read and a write 150 fields deep through a View: one E0368 (the depth
//    of one selector chain is bounded by the checker's recursion over the
//    expression itself, which is not part of this analysis);
//  - 1500 type switches, each with a direct write into the box (E0354) and a
//    write behind a pointer the box holds (E0368).
// The same output, in the same order, with 8 threads checking the bodies.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-view-stress.py all 1500 > %t.gopp
// RUN: not timeout 3 %gopp check -check-j=1 --check-error-limit=0 %t.gopp > %t.out 2>&1
// RUN: grep -o "error\[E[0-9]*\]" %t.out | sort | uniq -c | FileCheck --implicit-check-not=error %s
// RUN: not %gopp check -check-j=8 --check-error-limit=0 %t.gopp > %t.8.out 2>&1
// RUN: diff %t.out %t.8.out
// CHECK: {{^ *}}1500 error{{\[}}E0354]
// CHECK-NEXT: {{^ *}}4501 error{{\[}}E0368]
// CHECK-EMPTY:
package main
